
/*
 * This tsconfig is used for TypeScript projects created with `spacetimedb init
 * --lang typescript`. You can modify it as needed for your project, although
 * some options are required by SpacetimeDB.
 *
 * The 1.x/2.x split with the repository root is deliberate, not drift.
 *
 *   this module   spacetimedb ^1.11.2   locked 1.11.4   server runtime
 *   repository    spacetimedb ^2.10.1   locked 2.10.1   browser bindings
 *
 * The root depends on the SDK for `src/lib/spacetimedb/`, this module for the
 * server runtime, and the two are separate packages with separate lockfiles.
 * Nothing in the repository reconciles them, and they are not required to
 * agree — so treat the two majors as independent and keep both lockfiles.
 *
 * Upgrading this module to the 2.x SDK is a separate piece of work, not a
 * side effect of making it compile. Until then the source is written against
 * 1.x, and it resolves 1.x only when this directory has its own
 * `node_modules`. A `paths` mapping cannot enforce that: TypeScript treats
 * `paths` as substitutions to try first and falls back to standard resolution
 * when none match, so pinning the path still picks up the root's 2.x when the
 * install is missing. `npm run typecheck` therefore runs
 * `scripts/require-module-deps.mjs` first, which fails with the install
 * command instead of reporting six mis-resolutions as if they were defects in
 * `src/index.ts`.
 *
 * See docs/GLOBAL-CHAT.md and BUG-0591.
 */
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",

    /* The following options are required by SpacetimeDB
     * and should not be modified
     */
    "target": "ESNext",
    "lib": ["ES2021", "dom"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["./**/*"]
}